{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "template_id": "claude-binder-lane.v1",
  "base_profile": "small-run.template.json",
  "gap_notes": {
    "read_me": "This profile is the small run on user-owned Lambda Cloud compute. It inherits every scientific choice from small-run.template.json and replaces only the provider-facing adapter bindings. A value written __REQUIRED__ comes from the operator's own account. compose accepts those placeholders and materialize refuses them, so a run cannot start on an unread value.",
    "no_measured_rate": "No arm in this profile has a measured rate on Lambda Cloud. The three inherited fal prices are dropped rather than carried, because a rate measured on one provider loosens a ceiling by whatever the two providers differ by. Every arm here is unpriced, so qualify cannot quote the plan and budget_plan refuses to size one. That refusal is the correct state, not a defect. Record a rate from a single-candidate canary on your own Lambda Cloud account, then add a qualification block whose cost_basis.machine names that machine. references/measured-costs.md carries no Lambda Cloud row of any kind.",
    "backbone_generator": "The Lambda Cloud route generates with RFdiffusion, not RFdiffusion3. rfdiffusion3_generator.py reaches its model over an HTTPS deployment and requires --fal-url, so it has no container binding. This profile restores the RFdiffusion command that full-ensemble.template.json declares. --contigs stays __REQUIRED__ because the contig string describes one target and one binder length window.",
    "image_is_yours": "Lambda Cloud runs the operator's own container image. Modal profiles name bundled environments such as proteomics_gpu because the platform ships them. Nothing here ships an image, so --rfdiffusion-root, --weights-dir, --proteinmpnn-root and every container_image_digest are operator-resolved. Record the digest before the first job so the receipt names the bytes that ran.",
    "credentials": "lambda_platform declares no default credential variable, so the caller names one when it builds the account reader and the client handle. Both entry points in clients/lambda_client.py require that name and have no default. Export it in the session that dispatches. Do not write the key into this profile, a config file, or a note.",
    "control_builder": "control_builder.py runs the rescore arm as a child process rather than as its own stage, so the arm inherits whatever container the builder is in. The builder therefore carries the same predictor binding. Without it the control panel would fold on the session kernel, which has neither CUDA nor MPS.",
    "generator_identity": "This profile substitutes RFdiffusion for the RFdiffusion3 its base runs. The base reaches RFdiffusion3 over an HTTPS deployment, which no container route provides, so the generator here is RFdiffusion and the tool id says so. The adapter id stays rfdiffusion-generator because that names the backbone generator slot, not the tool filling it.",
    "provider_parameters": "`clients/lambda_client.py` ships and reads both of these values, so a handle refuses when either is absent or still __REQUIRED__. The client names no Lambda Cloud host, path, field, status word or authentication scheme, because nothing in this package records one, so the caller supplies three provider calls as a LambdaTransport. These two names remain what a Lambda instance launch is assumed to need. Confirm them against Lambda's own API before a first run."
  },
